  "releaseNotes": "# AID v2.0.1\n\n## 中文发布说明\n\n### 修复与优化\n\n- Skill 调用在余额不足时直接提示“账户余额不足”，不再误报为“理解请求失败”或“系统繁忙”，同时保留稳定的内部错误码供任务恢复与诊断使用。\n- 恢复“我的作品”和创作流程中的流程画布入口，补齐作品/剧集绑定、流程连线、节点编辑、右键菜单和视频导出，并保留节点主图、输入面板跟随和空格平移保护。\n- 素材准备中的场景、角色、道具列表为空时允许直接手动添加；同步或添加期间保持操作保护，避免重复创建。\n- 修复首页壳层重复切换后浮层挂载竞争、透明遮罩残留或导航失效的问题；登录、开源信息、交流群和用户菜单统一使用独立 Portal 容器。\n- 修复音画同步列表在高分辨率下视频区域与行内内容被裁切的问题，并让场景角色道具图、分镜图、分镜视频和音画同步编辑器按可用视口等比适配。\n- 修正登录弹窗背景显示，避免弹窗适配容器出现底色不一致。\n\n### 数据库与兼容性\n\n- 本版本不包含数据库结构或初始化数据变更，不需要新增升级 SQL；从 `v2.0.0` 升级时无需重复执行 `sql/v2.0.0.sql`。\n- 服务端接口与现有任务、计费及 Skill Run 数据保持兼容；Web 更新只影响静态资源和交互展示。\n\n### 升级注意事项\n\n- 升级前建议备份数据库、部署配置、证书和用户媒体目录。\n- Web 静态资源更新后如仍显示旧页面，请强制刷新浏览器或清理站点缓存。\n\n## English Release Notes\n\n### Fixes and Improvements\n\n- Skill invocations now report insufficient funds as “Account balance insufficient” instead of a misleading request-understanding or system-busy error, while preserving stable internal error codes for recovery and diagnostics.\n- Restored the flow-canvas entry points in My Works and the creation workflow, including project or episode binding, edges, node editing, context menus, video export, primary-node media, dock tracking, and guarded spacebar panning.\n- Empty scene, character, and prop preparation lists now allow direct manual creation while retaining duplicate-action protection during synchronization and submission.\n- Fixed portal ownership races after repeated home-shell navigation that could leave transparent overlays or unresponsive navigation. Login, open-source information, community, and user-menu overlays now share a dedicated portal root.\n- Fixed clipped video and inline content in high-resolution dubbing rows, and proportionally adapted scene, character, prop, storyboard-image, storyboard-video, and dubbing editors to the available viewport.\n- Corrected the login-dialog background so the fitted container renders with a consistent surface color.\n\n### Database and Compatibility\n\n- This release contains no database schema or initialization-data changes and requires no new migration. Upgrading from `v2.0.0` does not require rerunning `sql/v2.0.0.sql`.\n- Server APIs remain compatible with existing task, billing, and Skill Run data. Web changes are limited to static assets and interaction behavior.\n\n### Upgrade Notes\n\n- Back up the database, deployment configuration, certificates, and user media before upgrading.\n- If the previous Web interface remains visible after upgrading, perform a hard refresh or clear the site cache.",
